COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[84,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nFrom this verse, compile a list of the qualities of righteous women, and circulate around in a message for the benefit of women.\nEngage in reconciling two discordant spouses, in accordance with the Almighty's saying.\nSupplicate Allah for your parents and neighbors, as it is one of the greatest acts of kindness to them.\nguid\nAllah has entrusted you with a group of people; so be keen to implement Allah's command regarding them.\nConceit and boastfulness are not traits of Muslims, so avoid them.\nStinginess is a censured trait, and it is even worse when it is combined with promoting stinginess.\nrefl\nٱلرِّجَالُ قَوَّٰمُونَ عَلَى ٱلنِّسَآءِ بِمَا فَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ بَعۡضَهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ\nMen excel women in many ways; for example, positions of political authority are only for men, as is Prophethood. Moreover, men are singled out, to the exclusion of women, for many acts of worship, such as Jihad and Eid and Friday prayers. It is also because Allah has bestowed on them wisdom, mature thinking, patience and perseverance; the like of which women may not have. Men also have the exclusive obligation of spending on their wives. In fact, many types of spending are demanded exclusively of men, which distinct them from women. Al-Saadi: 177.\nMention three ways in which Allah distinguished men from women?\nفَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ قَٰنِتَٰتٌ حَٰفِظَٰتٞ لِّلۡغَيۡبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ ٱللَّهُۚ\nRighteous women are obedient to their husbands, or obedient to the command of Allah in fulfilling the rights of their husbands. (Guarding in absence) that is: The wife guards everything of which her husband is not aware, which includes guarding her chastity, her husband's property and secrets. (What Allah would have them guard) meaning: With Allah's protection, or with His command to women to obey and preserve their husbands. Ibn Juzay: 1/188.\nWhat are the qualities of righteous women?\nحَٰفِظَٰتٞ لِّلۡغَيۡبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ ٱللَّهُۚ\nThis is due to Allah's protection and guidance; they could not do it without His help, because the human soul is prone to evil. But whoever puts his trust in Allah, He will suffice him in whatever concerns him of his religious and worldly affairs. Al-Saadi: 177.\nWhy is women's guarding is constrained by the guarding of Allah?\nفَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ قَٰنِتَٰتٌ حَٰفِظَٰتٞ لِّلۡغَيۡبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ ٱللَّهُۚ\nRighteous women protect themselves and their chastity in the absence of their husbands, as well as what must be preserved in themselves and wealth. Moreover, they are guardians of their husbands' secrets, that is: what occurs between them in private. Al-Alusi: 5/24.\nWhat is inferred from describing righteous women as (guarding in absence)?\nفَإِنۡ أَطَعۡنَكُمۡ فَلَا تَبۡغُواْ عَلَيۡهِنَّ سَبِيلًاۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيّٗا كَبِيرٗا ٣٤\nYou should overlook your wives' faults and pardon them if they repent, or else, Allah is most Capable of punishing you because He does not like injustice done to anyone. Moreover, even with Allah's highness and greatness, He has not burdened you with more than you can bear, so likewise do not burden them with more than they can bear. Al-Alusi: 5/26.\nWhat is inferred from ending the verse with: (Allah is Most High, All-Great)?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيّٗا كَبِيرٗا ٣٤\nA threatening reminder for men that if they oppress their wives without reason, then Allah, the Most High, the Great, is their Protector, and He will take revenge on those who oppress and transgress against them. Ibn Kathir: 1/467.\nWhy does the verse conclude with the description of the Most High, the Great?\nوَٱعۡبُدُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَلَا تُشۡرِكُواْ بِهِۦ شَيۡـٔٗاۖ وَبِٱلۡوَٰلِدَيۡنِ إِحۡسَٰنٗا\nScholars said: After Allah, the great Benefactor, come the worthiest of all people of gratitude, obedience and benevolence are those whom Allah made kindness to them as an act of worship to Him, and showing gratitude to them as offering gratitude to Him. They are the parents. Al-Qurtubi: 6/302.\nAfter Allah, the Almighty, who is most deserving of thanks?\nwords\nنُشُوزَهُنَّArrogance and ill-conduct\nوَالجَار الجُنُبِNon-relative neighbors\nوَالصَّاحِبِ بِالجَنبِCompanions in travel and at home\nمُختَالًاConceited"],[85,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nGive to charity privately today, even if it is a little.\nReflect on this verse, and remember the tears of your beloved, the Prophet (r).\nLearn today the rules of dry ablution (Tayammum).\nguid\nDo not belittle a small good deed, and never underestimate a small bad deed.\nA day will come when all those who disobeyed the Messenger (r) will regret it, so be keen to follow him to avoid being like them.\nThe ease of Sharia is manifested in allowing Tayammum when water is missing.\nrefl\nوَإِن تَكُ حَسَنَةٗ يُضَٰعِفۡهَا وَيُؤۡتِ مِن لَّدُنۡهُ أَجۡرًا عَظِيمٗا ٤٠\nAbu Huraira (t) said: \"When Allah says, (a great reward), then who can measure that?\" Al-Qurtubi: 6/324.\nAllah says: (a great reward), what does that indicate?\nوَإِن تَكُ حَسَنَةٗ يُضَٰعِفۡهَا\nHe will multiply it tenfold or more, according to the nature of the deed and how beneficial it was, and according to the situation of the doer in terms of sincerity, love and righteousness. Al-Saadi: 179.\nWhat makes the multiplication of rewards for good deeds vary?\nفَكَيۡفَ إِذَا جِئۡنَا مِن كُلِّ أُمَّةِۢ بِشَهِيدٖ وَجِئۡنَا بِكَ عَلَىٰ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ شَهِيدٗا ٤١\nThe Prophet (r)said to Ibn Masoud: \"Recite the Quran to me.\" He said: How will I recite it to you when it was revealed to you?\" He said, \"I love to hear it recited by others.\" So, I recited Surat-An-Nisa' to him until I reached this verse: (How will it be when We bring a witness from every nation, and bring you (O Prophet) as a witness against these (people)). The Prophet (r) said: \"That is enough.\" I looked at him and saw his eyes overflowing with tears. Ibn Taimyah: 2/249.\nWhy did the Prophet's (r) eyes overflow with tears when he heard this verse?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنتُمۡ سُكَٰرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَعۡلَمُواْ مَا تَقُولُونَ\nThis indicates that the person praying should guard against what distracts him and occupies his heart, and that he should purify himself from what defiles it, because if purifying the body is obligatory, then purifying the heart is more important. If the place of prayer is protected from someone who has become impure, then it is clearly a priority to protect the heart from impure thoughts. Al-Alusi: 5/401.\nWhat does the prohibition of approaching prayer while drunk symbolize?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَقۡرَبُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنتُمۡ سُكَٰرَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَعۡلَمُواْ مَا تَقُولُونَ\nWe may also understand from the meaning of the verse that it is not allowed to start praying when one is extremely drowsy, to the point that he is not aware of what he is saying and doing. Indeed, it may indicate that the one who wants to pray should deal with anything that is distracting him, such as resisting the urge to use the toilet, craving for food and the like. Al-Saadi: 179.\nThe verse indicates that whoever wants to pray must clear his mind. Explain.\nفَتَيَمَّمُواْ صَعِيدٗا طَيِّبٗا فَٱمۡسَحُواْ بِوُجُوهِكُمۡ وَأَيۡدِيكُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُورًا ٤٣\nI believe that the wisdom of its enactment is to establish the necessity of purity in the hearts of believers, and to establish the sanctity of prayer, and to elevate its importance in their hearts, leaving them no situation in which they consider themselves to be praying without. This emphasizes the importance of communing with Allah. Ibn Ashur: 5/69.\nWhat is the wisdom behind the legislation of Tayammum for purity?\nفَتَيَمَّمُواْ صَعِيدٗا طَيِّبٗا فَٱمۡسَحُواْ بِوُجُوهِكُمۡ وَأَيۡدِيكُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُورًا ٤٣\nHis saying: (Allah is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving) is a conclusion to the ruling of the concession, as He pardoned the Muslims and did not require them to wash or perform ablution when sick, nor did He wait for the availability of water when it was not available, so that the prayers would become numerous and it would be difficult for them to make up for them. Ibn Ashur: 5/71.\nThis verse concludes with (Allah is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving). Why?\nwords\nتَكُThere is\nعَابِرِي سَبِيلٍPassing through a mosque\nلاَمَستُمُYou had intercourse with your wives\nفَتَيَمَّمُواSeek\nصَعِيدًاSand or dust on top of the earth\nطَيِّبًاPure"],[86,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn against swearing by other than Allah, such as swearing by the Prophet (r), or by the covenant and the like.\nSay, \"O Allah! grant my soul its piety and purify it, as You are the Best to purify it.\"\nIdentify an injustice you have suffered and seek help from your Lord alone, saying: O Helper, help me.\"\nguid\nWhoever distorts the meanings of the Holy Quran, resembles the Jews and Christians.\nWhoever seeks to know the truth must be polite with scholars and preachers, improve the wording of his questions, and be courteous to them.\nSins may be forgiven by Allah through repentance, or expiated by good deeds, or forgiven by Allah Almighty out of His grace and mercy. As for shirk, (associating partners with Allah), it is not forgiven, so beware of it.\nrefl\nوَٱللَّهُ أَعۡلَمُ بِأَعۡدَآئِكُمۡۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ وَلِيّٗا وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ نَصِيرٗا ٤٥\n(And Allah knows best your enemies), He knows your enemy better than you, so do not seek advice from them, as they are your enemies. (Allah is sufficient as a Helper, and Allah is sufficient as a Protector). Al-Baghawi: 1/542.\nThis verse forbids us from doing something. What is it?\nوَٱللَّهُ أَعۡلَمُ بِأَعۡدَآئِكُمۡۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ وَلِيّٗا وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ نَصِيرٗا ٤٥\nDo not give heed nor think about them. (Allah is sufficient as a Protector), He takes care of your needs as He wills. (And Allah is sufficient as a Helper), He repels their evil plots against you, so be content with His protection and help, and never pay attention to them nor be distressed by their evil plots. Al-Alusi: 5/45.\nWhat is the aim of informing the believers of Allah's help and protection?\nمِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَادُواْ يُحَرِّفُونَ ٱلۡكَلِمَ عَن مَّوَاضِعِهِۦ وَيَقُولُونَ سَمِعۡنَا وَعَصَيۡنَا\nThis is how they deal with knowledge, in the worst manner, by overturning truths, and applying true description to falsehood, thus denying that truth. With regard to how they act in terms of deeds and submission, they say, (We hear and we disobey). Al-Saadi: 181.\nJews are the worst people when it comes to knowledge and practice. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ ءَامِنُواْ بِمَا نَزَّلۡنَا مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا مَعَكُم مِّن قَبۡلِ أَن نَّطۡمِسَ وُجُوهٗا فَنَرُدَّهَا عَلَىٰٓ أَدۡبَارِهَآ\nImam Malik (r) said: \"The conversion of Ka'b Al-Ahbar (a Jewish rabbi) to Islam began when he passed by a man at night who was reciting this verse: (O you who were given the Scripture, believe...), so he put his hands over his face, and walked backward to his house and decided to accept Islam at once. Then he said: By Allah, , I feared that I would not reach my house until my face was obliterated.\" Al-Qurtubi: 6/404.\nWhat was the effect of this verse on Ka'b Al-Ahbar (r) when he heard it?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ يُزَكُّونَ أَنفُسَهُمۚ بَلِ ٱللَّهُ يُزَكِّي مَن يَشَآءُ وَلَا يُظۡلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا ٤٩ ٱنظُرۡ كَيۡفَ يَفۡتَرُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَۖ\nThis is the worst way of fabricating lies against Allah, because the implication of their self-praise is to say that Allah has made what they are following true and what the believing Muslims are following is false, and this is the greatest lie, which overturns facts by regarding truth as falsehood and falsehood as truth. Al-Saadi: 182.\nHow was their self-praise a fabrication of lies against Allah?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ يُزَكُّونَ أَنفُسَهُمۚ بَلِ ٱللَّهُ يُزَكِّي مَن يَشَآءُ وَلَا يُظۡلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا ٤٩\nThe above verse and this verse: (do not claim purity for yourselves) [53:32] require that one should disregard anyone who praises himself with his tongue, and that the one who is praised is the one whose deeds are good and who has been praised by Allah, the Almighty. Therefore, there is no consideration for a person's self-praise, but rather the consideration is Allah's purification of him. Al-Qurtubi: 6/407-408.\nWho is the truly pure servant?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ نَصِيبٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡجِبۡتِ وَٱلطَّٰغُوتِ وَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ أَهۡدَىٰ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ سَبِيلًا ٥١\n(Jibt): Magic. (Taghoot), the devil and the idol. This is the case with many of those who claim to belong to this religion, who glorify magic and shirk (worshiping idols beside Allah), and favor the disbelievers over many of the believers who adhere to the Sharia. Ibn Taimyah: 2/266.\nExplain the risk of shirk and magic to the Muslim Ummah?\nwords\nوَاسمَع غَيرَ مُسمَعٍ(ﷺ) The Jews imprecated deafness on the Prophet\nوَرَاعِنَاUnderstand from us and clarify to us\nلَيًّا بِأَلسِنَتِهِمTwisted their tongues to use a derogatory word"],[87,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you the knowledge of the Quran and Sunnah along with wisdom.\nSupplicate Allah for a Muslim who has been given a favor from Allah to have it blessed, and ask Allah to grant you a better one.\nRead about the virtue and rulings of fulfilling a trust so you can act upon it.\nguid\nWhoever is cursed by Allah is the wretched one who will never succeed, even if he attains the world's pleasures, so beware of the causes of Allah's curse.\nBeware of the temptation of women in this life, and know that women of Paradise are purer and more honorable than the forbidden ones in this life.\nObedience to Allah and His Messenger (r) is absolute while obedience to those in authority is conditional upon the obedience to Allah .\nrefl\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ وَمَن يَلۡعَنِ ٱللَّهُ فَلَن تَجِدَ لَهُۥ نَصِيرًا ٥٢\n(Those are the ones): Those who have been described as having received a portion of the Scripture believe in jibt and taghoot. (Whom Allah has cursed), Allah says that He Has disgraced them, and cast them out of His mercy because of their belief in jibt and taghoot, and their disbelief in Allah and His Messenger in defiance to Allah and His Messenger. Al-Tabari: 8/471.\nWhen does the knowledge of the Scripture become useful?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا سَوۡفَ نُصۡلِيهِمۡ نَارٗا كُلَّمَا نَضِجَتۡ جُلُودُهُم بَدَّلۡنَٰهُمۡ جُلُودًا غَيۡرَهَا\nSince the fire -as we know it- is annihilating and destroying, He resumed His statement in response to that: (Whenever their skins are burnt through), became dead skins with no feeling, (We will replace them), we will make for them (other skins) instead of the burnt ones, by returning them to what they were. The repetition of torment is an appropriate recompense for their repeated denial of Allah's message. Al-Biqai: 2/269.\nThe disbelievers' skins will be replaced in Hellfire. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ سَنُدۡخِلُهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۖ لَّهُمۡ فِيهَآ أَزۡوَٰجٞ مُّطَهَّرَةٞۖ وَنُدۡخِلُهُمۡ ظِلّٗا ظَلِيلًا ٥٧\n(Deepening shade): Is continuous without opening, spread out with no confinement, permanent with no sun blaze, and never hot or cold, rather it is very moderate. Al-Biqai: 2/270.\nWhat does (Deepening shade) in Paradise mean?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأۡمُرُكُمۡ أَن تُؤَدُّواْ ٱلۡأَمَٰنَٰتِ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهَا وَإِذَا حَكَمۡتُم بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِ أَن تَحۡكُمُواْ بِٱلۡعَدۡلِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُم بِهِۦٓۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ سَمِيعَۢا بَصِيرٗا ٥٨\nRulers must rule only with justice. (Justice) is what Allah had revealed as He says, (Indeed, Allah commands you to return trusts to their owners, and when you judge between people, judge with justice. What an excellent exhortation from Allah to you! Indeed, Allah is All-Hearing, All-Seeing). Ibn Taimyah: 2/272.\nWhat is meant by (justice) in this verse?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱلرَّسُولَ وَأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِ مِنكُمۡۖ\nObeying those in authority is on the condition that they do not enjoin disobedience to Allah; if they do so, then there should not be any obedience to any created being if it involves disobedience toward the Creator. Perhaps this is the reason why the verb (obey) is not repeated with regard to those who are in authority, but it is mentioned with regard to the Messenger (r). That is because the Messenger (r) only enjoins obedience to Allah, and whoever obeys him has obeyed Allah. Al-Saadi: 184.\nWhy is the verb (obey) mentioned with regard to the Messenger (r), but omitted with regard to those who are in authority?\nوَأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِ مِنكُمۡۖ\nPeople's religious and worldly affairs cannot be put right except by obeying those who are in authority. Al-Saadi: 183.\nWhy is it a duty to obey those who are in authority?\nفَإِن تَنَٰزَعۡتُمۡ فِي شَيۡءٖ فَرُدُّوهُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَٱلرَّسُولِ إِن كُنتُمۡ تُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۚ ذَٰلِكَ خَيۡرٞ وَأَحۡسَنُ تَأۡوِيلًا ٥٩\n(Refer it to Allah and the Messenger): Referring it to Allah is by looking into His Book (the Holy Quran), and referring it to His Messenger (r) is by asking him during his life, and looking into his Sunnah after his death. Ibn Juzay: 1/196.\nHow can disagreements be referred to Allah and His Messenger (r)?\nwords\nنَقِيرًاA speck on a date seed\nظَلِيلًاDense permanent shade\nنِعِمَّاWhat an excellent\nتَأوِيلًاThe end result"],[88,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to help you become an effective and influential preacher and grant you far-reaching speech, then begin acting on this duty.\nRecall a sin that you had committed in the past, then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nLearn the reason of revelation of this verse, reflect on that and draw useful lessons from it, then share them in a message with those around you.\nguid\nResorting to other than the Holy Quran and Sunnah is a peril, even in the smallest matters.\nTurning away from the rules of Sharia is the manner of hypocrites.\nIt is recommended to turn away from those with sick hearts, and to admonish them with a far-reaching words that touch their hearts.\nrefl\nوَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمۡ تَعَالَوۡاْ إِلَىٰ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ وَإِلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ رَأَيۡتَ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ يَصُدُّونَ عَنكَ صُدُودٗا ٦١ فَكَيۡفَ إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتۡهُم مُّصِيبَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ ثُمَّ جَآءُوكَ يَحۡلِفُونَ بِٱللَّهِ إِنۡ أَرَدۡنَآ إِلَّآ إِحۡسَٰنٗا وَتَوۡفِيقًا ٦٢\nWhen these hypocrites were called to what Allah revealed and to His Messenger -after his death, coming to the Messenger means following his Sunnah- they turned away and said: \"In taking this way, we intended good by words and deeds, and reconciliation between evidence through reason and Sharia.\" Ibn Taimyah: 2/286.\nWhat are the similarities between past hypocrites and contemporary hypocrites?\nفَكَيۡفَ إِذَآ أَصَٰبَتۡهُم مُّصِيبَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ ثُمَّ جَآءُوكَ يَحۡلِفُونَ بِٱللَّهِ إِنۡ أَرَدۡنَآ إِلَّآ إِحۡسَٰنٗا وَتَوۡفِيقًا ٦٢\nThis verse is evidence that an adversity may befall a person due to sins he has committed. Al-Alusi: 5/69.\nCan sins be the cause of an adversity? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَقُل لَّهُمۡ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَوۡلَۢا بَلِيغٗا ٦٣\nMeaning: Advise them in private, between you and them, for that is more likely to succeed in achieving the desired goal. Al-Saadi: 184.\nWhy is private advice better than public advice?\nفَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ وَعِظۡهُمۡ وَقُل لَّهُمۡ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَوۡلَۢا بَلِيغٗا ٦٣\nThis proves that the one who commits sins, even if he is to be overlooked publicly, is to be admonished privately in the sternest terms, in whatever manner is thought most likely to achieve the goal. Al-Saadi: 184.\nYou may turn away from a sinner for a reason, but how should you deal with him?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَعۡلَمُ ٱللَّهُ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ فَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ وَعِظۡهُمۡ وَقُل لَّهُمۡ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَوۡلَۢا بَلِيغٗا ٦٣\nAbu Ja'far said: \"This is an allusion from Allah to these hypocrites that their disobedience to Allah and His Messenger, and their discontent with His Messenger's judgment is due to Allah's abandonment of them and the prevailing of wretchedness over them. If it were not for that, they would have been among those who were content with the Messenger's judgment and hasten to obey him.\" Al-Tabari: 8/516.\nWhat prevented the hypocrites from accepting the judgment of Allah and His Messenger?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَعۡلَمُ ٱللَّهُ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ فَأَعۡرِضۡ عَنۡهُمۡ وَعِظۡهُمۡ وَقُل لَّهُمۡ فِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَوۡلَۢا بَلِيغٗا ٦٣\nMeaning: We have not sent you and other Messengers except to be kind to the people, to forgive and pray for them with the utmost effort and sincerity. Al-Biqai: 2/274.\nThere is a condition for preaching that yields acceptance from Allah and from people. What is it?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ إِذ ظَّلَمُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ جَآءُوكَ فَٱسۡتَغۡفَرُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱسۡتَغۡفَرَ لَهُمُ ٱلرَّسُولُ لَوَجَدُواْ ٱللَّهَ تَوَّابٗا رَّحِيمٗا ٦٤\nThis coming to the Messenger (r) was applicable only during his life, as the context indicates that, since the Messenger's prayers for forgiveness could only happen during his life. After his death, nothing is asked of him, rather that is ascribing partners to Allah (shirk). Al-Saadi: 185.\nWhen is it appropriate to come to the Messenger (r) to ask him for prayer for Allah's forgiveness?\nwords\nالطَّاغُوتِFalsehood, not ordained by Allah\nحَرَجًاDiscomfort"],[89,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nListen to a sermon or lecture and practice what you learned, unlike the hypocrites who do not act according to what they are preached.\nRecall a sermon or advice that you heard and act on it today.\nTake the initiative to respond to the caller: \"Come to prayer.\"\nguid\nOne of the ways to remain steadfast in religion is to do what you are preached and reminded of.\nDoing good deeds is a mere favor from Allah, so ask Him to bless you with it.\nDiscouraging others from doing good deeds is a habit of hypocrites, so beware of discouraging someone from doing good.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّا كَتَبۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَنِ ٱقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡ أَوِ ٱخۡرُجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِكُم مَّا فَعَلُوهُ إِلَّا قَلِيلٞ مِّنۡهُمۡۖ\nAllah states that if He were to instruct them to do something that people find very difficult, such as killing themselves or leaving their homes, none would do it except a few of them. Therefore, they should be grateful to Him that what He has instructed them to do is easy for everyone, and is not difficult to do. This indicates that one should think of the hardships and difficulties that Allah could have put him through, so that he will realize that the enjoined acts of worship are in fact very easy. Al-Saadi: 185.\nHow do you deduce from this verse the ease and tolerance of Sharia?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّا كَتَبۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَنِ ٱقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡ أَوِ ٱخۡرُجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِكُم مَّا فَعَلُوهُ إِلَّا قَلِيلٞ مِّنۡهُمۡۖ\nAllah states that, by His grace, He did not prescribe this for us, lest our sins become apparent, for how many lighter instructions we fell short of fulfilling, so how will it be with this hard one? But by Allah, the immigrant Companions left their homes desolate in search of a pleasant life. Al-Qurtubi: 6/446.\nExplain how Allah, graciously, did not burden His servants with hard duties.\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّهُمۡ فَعَلُواْ مَا يُوعَظُونَ بِهِۦ لَكَانَ خَيۡرٗا لَّهُمۡ وَأَشَدَّ تَثۡبِيتٗا ٦٦\nIf a servant practices what he knows, Allah will grant him knowledge of what he does not know, as He says, (But if they did what they were instructed, it would surely be better for them and more reassuring). Ibn Taimyah: 2/293.\nPracticing the knowledge is a reason for gaining more of it. Explain in light of this verse.\nذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَضۡلُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ عَلِيمٗا ٧٠\nMeaning: This great bounty comes from Allah, and not anyone else; or it comes from Allah and not merited by the deeds of the servants. (And sufficient is Allah as Knower): He Knows the reward of those who obey Him, the measure of the bounty, and the merit of its recipients. Al-Alusi: 5/79.\nWhat is inferred from describing Allah as (The Knower)? What is its effect?\nذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَضۡلُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِۚ وَكَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ عَلِيمٗا ٧٠\nThis affirms that they did not attain this bounty through their obedience, but by the grace of Allah Almighty. Al-Baghawi: 1/560.\nDid the believers attain this bounty through their obedience?\nوَإِنَّ مِنكُمۡ لَمَن لَّيُبَطِّئَنَّ فَإِنۡ أَصَٰبَتۡكُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَالَ قَدۡ أَنۡعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيَّ إِذۡ لَمۡ أَكُن مَّعَهُمۡ شَهِيدٗا ٧٢\n(He who lingers behind) that is: He is reluctant to engage in Jihad due to his weak faith or hypocrisy, and he orders others to do so with an emphatic command, showing compassion for them, which is the essence of deception, as this lingering results in weakness causing enemy's baldness that leads to the eventual demise of Muslims. Al-Biqai: 2/278.\nIf one lingers behind and not participate in Jihad or doing good, what will that lead to?\nوَإِنَّ مِنكُمۡ لَمَن لَّيُبَطِّئَنَّ فَإِنۡ أَصَٰبَتۡكُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَالَ قَدۡ أَنۡعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيَّ إِذۡ لَمۡ أَكُن مَّعَهُمۡ شَهِيدٗا ٧٢\nMeaning: He discourages others from participating in Jihad. It is also said that he himself is reluctant to engage in Jihad. (And if disaster strikes you) such as death and defeat. This hypocrite is pleased to be absent from the believers if they are defeated. Ibn Juzay: 1/198.\nThis verse reveals two traits of hypocrites. What are they ?\nwords\nوَأَشَدَّ تَثبِيتًاAnd more reassuring for their faith\nثُبَاتٍA group after group\nلَيُبَطِّئَنَّHe who lingers behind\nشَهِيدًاOne who is present\nيَشرُونَThey sell"],[90,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nToday, think about the plight of the vulnerable and displaced believers, and donate to their cause while praying often for them.\nList three reasons why satan's plot is weak.\nThink of three people you know who died suddenly.\nguid\nWhether he is killed or victorious, the fighter in cause of Allah receives the best deal, which is the pleasure of Allah Almighty.\nThe devil's plot is weak that anyone can repel and nullify by remembering Allah, blowing his breath to his left side, and by adhering to the Holy Quran and the authentic prophetic Sunnah.\nBeing cautious will not save one from his fate.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُقَٰتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُقَٰتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱلطَّٰغُوتِ\nThe individual's participation in Jihad is commensurate with his level of faith in Allah, sincerity and commitment. Jihad in Allah's cause is one of the signs, requirements and results of faith, just as fighting in the cause of taghoot is one of the signs and results of disbelief. Al-Saadi: 187.\nHow is faith related to Jihad?\nفَقَٰتِلُوٓاْ أَوْلِيَآءَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنِ ۖ إِنَّ كَيْدَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنِ كَانَ ضَعِيفًا ٧٦\nAllah describes them as (weak) since they do not fight hoping for reward, nor they abandon fighting out of fear of punishment. Rather, they fight out of haughtiness or envy of the believers for what Allah has given them of His bounty. In contrast, the believers fight hoping for Allah's great reward, and they abandon fighting out of fear of His punishment. So, the believer fights with insight into what he will have with Allah if he is killed, and what he will have of spoils and victory if he is safe. The disbeliever fights out of fear of being killed and despair of resurrection. Al-Tabari: 8/547.\nAllah describes the plot of satan and his allies as (weak). Why ?\nإِنَّ كَيْدَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنِ كَانَ ضَعِيفًا ٧٦\nThe plot of satan is his scheme, which is manifested in the plot of his allies against Muslims to turn people against them. Ibn Ashur: 5/124.\nWhat is meant by the plot of satan?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ قِيلَ لَهُمۡ كُفُّوٓاْ أَيۡدِيَكُمۡ وَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتُواْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡقِتَالُ إِذَا فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ يَخۡشَوۡنَ ٱلنَّاسَ كَخَشۡيَةِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡ أَشَدَّ خَشۡيَةٗۚ\nThe command to establish prayer and pay zakah is to alert them that striving against oneself precedes Jihad against the disbelievers. Unless a Muslim is able to submit to Allah's command to be generous with money, he will hardly be able to be generous with his soul, for being generous with one's soul is the ultimate form of generosity. Al-Alusi: 5/85.\nWhy is the command to pray and give zakah precedes the command to fight?\nوَقَالُواْ رَبَّنَا لِمَ كَتَبۡتَ عَلَيۡنَا ٱلۡقِتَالَ لَوۡلَآ أَخَّرۡتَنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ قَرِيبٖۗ قُلۡ مَتَٰعُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا قَلِيلٞ وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ خَيۡرٞ لِّمَنِ ٱتَّقَىٰ وَلَا تُظۡلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا ٧٧\nMeaning: Even if Allah extended your lifespans until you become tired of life, it will still be short because every temporary thing is little. Moreover, attaining its pleasures is not certain, and if they are attained, they will be marred by discomforts. Al-Biqai: 2/283.\nIs longevity a cause of happiness after all?\nقُلۡ مَتَٰعُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا قَلِيلٞ وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةُ خَيۡرٞ لِّمَنِ ٱتَّقَىٰ وَلَا تُظۡلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا ٧٧\nThe enjoyment of this world is enjoying its benefits and pleasures. It is described as (little) because it will perish, and the Prophet (r) said: \"This world and I are just like a rider who rested beneath the shade of a tree then went and left it.\" Al-Qurtubi: 6/463.\nWhy is the enjoyment of this life described as (little)?\nفَمَالِ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ لَا يَكَادُونَ يَفۡقَهُونَ حَدِيثٗا ٧٨\nThis is an implicit praise for the those who understand what Allah and His Messenger say, and it is encouragement to do so and to look for means that will help to attain that, such as focusing on their words and pondering them, and taking measures to understand them. Al-Saadi: 189.\nHow does this verse encourage seeking knowledge?\nwords\nالطَّاغُوتِTyranny and corruption\nفَتِيلًاA thread inside the seed of a date\nبُرُوجٍ مُشَيَّدَةٍFortified towers"],[91,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nStudy a verse from the Quran, by understanding its meaning, then by reflecting on what Allah intended from it, then act on that.\nPay a visit to an Islamic scholar, and ask him about some current controversial issues that you are facing in your life.\nHelp a needy person by interceding for him, and be rewarded by Allah.\nguid\nOne of the qualities of believers is patience and not rushing to convey news.\nInterceding in a good cause is a virtue, but interceding in an evil cause is a sin.\nResponding to a greeting with the same greeting is an obligation, and responding with a better one is recommended.\nrefl\nأَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَۚ\nOne of the benefits of reflecting upon the Book of Allah is that it causes the individual to become certain in faith and knowledge that it is the words of Allah. Al-Saadi: 190.\nWhat is the benefit of reflecting upon the Quran?\nأَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَۚ وَلَوۡ كَانَ مِنۡ عِندِ غَيۡرِ ٱللَّهِ لَوَجَدُواْ فِيهِ ٱخۡتِلَٰفٗا كَثِيرٗا ٨٢\nThe above verse and this verse (Then do they not reflect upon the Quran, or are there locks upon their hearts) [47:24] indicate that reflecting upon the Holy Quran to know its meanings is mandatory. Al-Qurtubi: 6/477.\nWhat is the ruling on reflecting upon the Holy Quran?\nأَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَۚ وَلَوۡ كَانَ مِنۡ عِندِ غَيۡرِ ٱللَّهِ لَوَجَدُواْ فِيهِ ٱخۡتِلَٰفٗا كَثِيرٗا ٨٢\nMeaning: A contradiction as in the speech of humans, or a variation in its level of eloquence, but the Holy Quran is impeccable which proves that it is the word of Allah. If one has doubts about something in the Quran, then he must question his own judgement, and ask scholars. He should study their writings until he comes to know that indeed the Holy Quran is free of contradictions. Ibn Juzay: 1/200.\nWhat one must do when he has doubts about something in the Holy Quran?\nمَّن يَشۡفَعۡ شَفَٰعَةً حَسَنَةٗ يَكُن لَّهُۥ نَصِيبٞ مِّنۡهَاۖ وَمَن يَشۡفَعۡ شَفَٰعَةٗ سَيِّئَةٗ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كِفۡلٞ مِّنۡهَاۗ\nExamples of interceding in a good cause are relieving a Muslim of distress, removing injustice, or bringing about a benefit for him. Interceding in an evil cause, however, is just the opposite of that. Al-Juzay: 1/201.\nGive some examples of interceding in a good cause and interceding in an evil one?\nمَّن يَشۡفَعۡ شَفَٰعَةً حَسَنَةٗ يَكُن لَّهُۥ نَصِيبٞ مِّنۡهَاۖ وَمَن يَشۡفَعۡ شَفَٰعَةٗ سَيِّئَةٗ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كِفۡلٞ مِّنۡهَاۗ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ مُّقِيتٗا ٨٥\nInterceding in a good cause is reconciliation between people, and interceding in an evil cause is spreading malicious gossip among people. Al-Baghawi: 1/568.\nWhat is interceding in a good cause and interceding in an evil one?\nوَإِذَا حُيِّيتُم بِتَحِيَّةٖ فَحَيُّواْ بِأَحۡسَنَ مِنۡهَآ أَوۡ رُدُّوهَآۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَسِيبًا ٨٦\nHow good it is that these verses follow the verse on Jihad, indicating that whoever offers peace, then we must stop fighting him, even in war. One of the implications of these two verses is that the structure of this Surah is based on encouraging kindness, compassion and communication, the greatest of which is gentle speech, because it reflects what is in the heart and manifests in intercession and greeting. Al-Biqai: 2/292.\nThe verses on intercession and greeting follow the verses on Jihad. Why?\nوَإِذَا حُيِّيتُم بِتَحِيَّةٖ فَحَيُّواْ بِأَحۡسَنَ مِنۡهَآ أَوۡ رُدُّوهَآۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٍ حَسِيبًا ٨٦\nThis is guidance to a type of noble morals and best of deeds. It means that if Allah bestows a favor upon you, then you should offer the best of it in His cause, give some of it to charity, and return some of it back to Allah through the needy. Indeed, Allah is the best of those who grant success. Al-Alusi: 5/104.\nWhat does it mean to respond with a better greeting?\nwords\nبَيَّتَConspires at night\nأَذَاعُوا بِهِThey spread it around\nتَنكِيلًاA punishment\nكِفلٌA portion of its burden\nمُقِيتًاA Watchful and a Keeper"],[92,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nSay: \"O Allah, make the best of my deeds the last of them, and the best of my days the day I meet You.\"\nThink of a particular act of worship that you wish to perform but could not; then recall a sin you committed, and ask often for Allah's forgiveness. Your sin was probably the reason for not being able to perform this worship act.\nShare a message in which you warn against what is in the hearts of hypocrites toward the believers.\nguid\nThere is no doubt that one day you will stand before Allah, so what have you prepared for that?\nDo not be surprised at the number of those who are misguided, for Allah knows who deserves guidance.\nThe ultimate aim of the people of hypocrisy and disbelief is that the believers become misguided and disbelievers.\nrefl\nٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَۚ لَيَجۡمَعَنَّكُمۡ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِۗ وَمَنۡ أَصۡدَقُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ حَدِيثٗا ٨٧\nA liar tells lies because he hopes to gain a benefit or to avert harm from himself. Allah, the Almighty, is the Creator of harm and benefit, so to even think that a lie may occur in His speech is inconceivable. Al-Tabari: 8/593.\nWhy is no one more truthful in speech than Allah?\nوَمَنۡ أَصۡدَقُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ حَدِيثٗا ٨٧\nAllah asserts that His word is of the highest level of truth. Anything that is said concerning belief, knowledge and deeds that is contrary to what Allah has told us is false, because it goes against the true and certain text, hence it cannot be true. Al-Saadi: 191.\nWhat is the difference between one who takes his beliefs and principles from the Quran and another who takes them from a different source?\nفَمَا لَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ فِئَتَيۡنِ وَٱللَّهُ أَرۡكَسَهُم بِمَا كَسَبُوٓاْۚ\nMeaning: Why have you divided into two groups over the hypocrites, and not agreed to disavow them? This question shows disapproval and negation, and the speech is addressed to all believers, but the meaning of the rebuke is directed to some of them who were inclined to the hypocrites and defending them, while others opposed the hypocrites and disowned them. So, the believers were forbidden from division, and were commanded to be all on one path in disowning the hypocrites, since the signs of their hypocrisy and disbelief are quite clear. Al-Qasimi: 1/200.\nWhat is the duty that Allah called upon believers to do in dealing with hypocrites?\nفَمَا لَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ فِئَتَيۡنِ وَٱللَّهُ أَرۡكَسَهُم بِمَا كَسَبُوٓاْۚ\nAllah has reverted the hypocrites to disbelief as recompense for their evil thoughts and insincerity toward His Messenger (r). Deeds lead to similar ones, so, good deeds bring more good deeds, and evil deeds result in worse deeds. Ibn Ashur: 5/150.\nWhy has Allah reverted the hypocrites to disbelief?\nفَلَا تَتَّخِذُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ\nThis necessitates that you should not love them, because alliances and friendships can only stem from love. Moreover, it entails that you should hate them, and regard them as enemies, because the prohibition on anything is a command to do its opposite. Al-Saadi: 192.\nWhat does the divine command of prohibiting taking hypocrites as allies entail?\nفَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَخُذُوهُمۡ وَٱقۡتُلُوهُمۡ حَيۡثُ وَجَدتُّمُوهُمۡۖ\n(If they turn away) meaning: They turn away from emigrating. This is a warning to them before are held accountable. Meaning: Inform them of this ruling, and if they reject it, then seize and kill them. This proves that if one does something that may constitute disbelief, he will not be held accountable for it until he is informed of its consequences. If he persists, then he must be prosecuted and given a chance to repent. Ibn Ashur: 5/152.\nFor one who does something that may constitute disbelief, when should he be held accountable for it?\nوَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَسَلَّطَهُمۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فَلَقَٰتَلُوكُمۡۚ\nAllah, the Almighty, empowers the polytheists to fight the believers by enabling and strengthening them, either as a punishment and retribution when evil is spread and sins become apparent, or to test the believers, or to expiate their sins. Al-Qurtubi: 6/511.\nSometimes, Allah empower the polytheists to fight the believers. Why?\nwords\nأَركَسَهُمReverted them\nحَصِرَت صُدُورُهُمTheir hearts strained at the prospect of fighting you\nالسَّلَمَYielding and compliance\nأُركِسُوا فِيهَاThey fell in a worst case\nثَقِفتُمُوهُمYou found them"],[93,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nList all punishments for killing a believer, then share them in a message or an article, warning against them.\nRecall a big sin that you had committed, then perform a big good deed and ask often for Allah's forgiveness so that He may grant you forgiveness.\nVerification of all matters is a likable method to Allah. Pick an event or a piece of news, verify it and share its truth in a message, reminding others of the importance of verification.\nguid\nLook at the enormity of the crime committed by the one who killed his fellow believer, and how Allah threatened him with great punishment, so how can some people be so careless about it?!\nA good Muslim shows mercy, offers advice, and seeks to guide those who are heedless and sinful, because he remembers that he was previously in their state or close to it.\nReflect on your condition before being guided, and how Allah blessed, favored, and honored you.\nrefl\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤۡمِنٍ أَن يَقۡتُلَ مُؤۡمِنًا إِلَّا خَطَٔاًۚ وَمَن قَتَلَ مُؤۡمِنًا خَطَٔاً فَتَحۡرِيرُ رَقَبَةٖ مُّؤۡمِنَةٖ وَدِيَةٞ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن يَصَّدَّقُواْۚ\nSince mistakes are forgiven according to Sharia, it was thought that there was nothing against one who made a mistake; however, this is not true in the case of accidental killing in order to preserve lives, for it is a very serious matter. Allah says, sternly, urging to take all precautions when dealing with anything that causes death. (Must free), it is obligatory upon him to free (a slave), a person in slavery. Al-Biqai: 2/297.\nAllah prescribes expiation and blood money in the case of accidental killing even though this Muslim Ummah is forgiven for its mistakes. Why?\nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤۡمِنٍ أَن يَقۡتُلَ مُؤۡمِنًا إِلَّا خَطَٔاًۚ\nThis confirms that this prohibition is very serious and that this action is diametrically opposed to faith. Indeed, such a thing can only be done by a disbeliever or an evil doer whose faith is sorely lacking, and for whom there is the fear of what is even worse than that. True faith prevents the believer from killing his brother with whom Allah has ordained the brotherhood of faith, which involves loving him, taking him as a close friend and ally, and protecting him from any harm; and what harm could be greater than killing? Al-Saadi: 192.\nWhy a true believer would not kill a fellow believer?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا ضَرَبۡتُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَتَبَيَّنُواْ وَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَنۡ أَلۡقَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكُمُ ٱلسَّلَٰمَ لَسۡتَ مُؤۡمِنٗا\nThis is a great approach toward understanding the laws of Sharia, namely that judgments are based on assumptions and appearances rather than on certainty and knowledge of the hidden. Al-Qurtubi: 7/51.\nThis verse contains a great path toward understanding the laws of Sharia. What is it?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا ضَرَبۡتُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَتَبَيَّنُواْ وَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَنۡ أَلۡقَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكُمُ ٱلسَّلَٰمَ لَسۡتَ مُؤۡمِنٗا\n(Make sure) seek with prudence to clarify matters, verify its occurrence with accuracy, distinguish between the truth and falsehood, and act only on what is clear to you. (And do not say) words, let alone action against one (who offers you) no matter who he is, (the greetings of peace), he initiated the offer of peace while giving in, (You are not a believer). Al-Biqai: 2/299.\nA sign of a sincere and wise believer is his prudence and verification before taking action. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تَقُولُواْ لِمَنۡ أَلۡقَىٰٓ إِلَيۡكُمُ ٱلسَّلَٰمَ لَسۡتَ مُؤۡمِنٗا تَبۡتَغُونَ عَرَضَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا\n(Seeking), desperately pursuing through killing. (The perishable goods of worldly life): By taking his possessions of worldly life, or retaliating for an old blood feud. Ibn Abbas (t) said: \"Some Muslim individuals caught up with a man who said to them: \"Peace be upon you,\" but they killed him and took his possessions. Thereupon this verse was revealed: (...seeking the perishable goods of worldly life)\". Al-Biqai: 2/299.\nThe spoils of war are a test of the fighter in the cause of Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nكَذَٰلِكَ كُنتُم مِّن قَبۡلُ فَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فَتَبَيَّنُوٓاْۚ\nThis is a great education for one to feel for others when holding them accountable for situations in which he was before, such as a teacher harshly censures a student when the student spared no effort. Likewise, it is great education for those who, when evaluating students of knowledge, are used to being strict with them seeking out their mistakes. Ibn Ashur: 5/168.\nWhat education can one learn from this verse: (You were in the same position before)?\nكَذَٰلِكَ كُنتُم مِّن قَبۡلُ فَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nMeaning: Just as He guided you after you had been astray, He may also guide others; just as guidance was a gradual process for you, it may also be like that for others. So, the one who is perfect should look at his original imperfect state, and think about how he should deal with those who are still like that, on the basis of what he knows about how he was before, and he should call them with wisdom and beautiful preaching. This is one of the most effective ways in which he may benefit himself and others. Al-Saadi: 195.\nThis verse contains a great rule for dealing with disobedient Muslims. Explain.\nwords\nضَرَبتُمGoing forth in land\nعَرَضَ الحَيَاةِPerishable goods of worldly life (spoils of war)"],[94,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah often for the mujahidin.\nSpend some of your money today for charity, and strive to do so in order to be one of those who fight with their wealth in the cause of Allah.\nSelect a good deed, intend to do it, and strive to achieve its objectives, for Allah will reward His servant and recompense him for his intention, even if he is unable to complete the deed.\nguid\nNot every weakness is excusable.\nReflect on the great mercy of Allah toward His servants, as He reassured the weak and excused with pardon and forgiveness.\nAn example of the ease of Sharia is shortening the prayer for the traveler, so be grateful to Allah for this blessing.\nrefl\nوَكُلّٗا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰۚ\nThis is how it is when one category of people is favored over another, and each of them has its own virtues; Allah mentions the good characteristics that they have in common lest anyone think that the one of lesser standing is being condemned. For this reason, Allah says here, (To each Allah has promised a fine reward). Al-Saadi: 195.\nAfter mentioning fighters, and those who stayed behind, Allah says, (To each Allah has promised a fine reward). What is inferred from that?\nفَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُجَٰهِدِينَ بِأَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ وَأَنفُسِهِمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡقَٰعِدِينَ دَرَجَةٗۚ وَكُلّٗا وَعَدَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰۚ وَفَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمُجَٰهِدِينَ عَلَى ٱلۡقَٰعِدِينَ أَجۡرًا عَظِيمٗا ٩٥ دَرَجَٰتٖ مِّنۡهُ وَمَغۡفِرَةٗ وَرَحۡمَةٗۚ\nConsider how well this transition from one state to a higher one in this verse, as it states first of all that the mujahid and a non-mujahid are not equal, then it states clearly that the mujahid is superior by one rank to the one who stays behind, then it moves on to favoring the mujahid with forgiveness, mercy and high status. Al-Saadi: 195.\nThe verse contains an attractive way of describing the reward of mujahideen. What is it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَوَفَّىٰهُمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ ظَالِمِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَالُواْ فِيمَ كُنتُمۡۖ قَالُواْ كُنَّا مُسۡتَضۡعَفِينَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ قَالُوٓاْ أَلَمۡ تَكُنۡ أَرۡضُ ٱللَّهِ وَٰسِعَةٗ فَتُهَاجِرُواْ فِيهَاۚ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مَأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ وَسَآءَتۡ مَصِيرًا ٩٧\nThis verse was revealed about a group of people from Makkah who had converted to Islam when the Messenger was in Makkah. When the Messenger (r) migrated, they stayed behind and were persecuted until they renounced their faith, and joined the polytheists against the Muslims in the battle of Badr and were killed as disbelievers. The Muslims said: \"Those were believers but were forced to renounce their faith and fight against us.\" So, this verse was revealed. [Narrated by Al-Bukhari on the authority of Ibn Abbas]. Ibn Ashur: 5/174.\nWhen is a Muslim excused for weakness?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَوَفَّىٰهُمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ ظَالِمِيٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ قَالُواْ فِيمَ كُنتُمۡۖ قَالُواْ كُنَّا مُسۡتَضۡعَفِينَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ قَالُوٓاْ أَلَمۡ تَكُنۡ أَرۡضُ ٱللَّهِ وَٰسِعَةٗ فَتُهَاجِرُواْ فِيهَاۚ\nMeaning: Were you not able to emigrate and distance yourself from those who oppressed you? This verse is evidence that migrating from a land in which sins are committed is an obligation. Al-Qurtubi: 7/64.\nWhat should a Muslim do if he lives in a city full of sins and fears for himself?\nوَمَن يُهَاجِرۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ يَجِدۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مُرَٰغَمٗا كَثِيرٗا وَسَعَةٗۚ وَمَن يَخۡرُجۡ مِنۢ بَيۡتِهِۦ مُهَاجِرًا إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ثُمَّ يُدۡرِكۡهُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ فَقَدۡ وَقَعَ أَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۗ\nAllah encourages the believers to migrate by mentioning the abundance and great reward in order to help them overcome the devil's whispers who may suggest that leaving the comfort of home would put them in the hardship of exile or death before reaching their destination. Al-Biqai: 2/299.\nWhat the whispers that satan stirs up to prevent the believer from emigrating?\nوَمَن يَخۡرُجۡ مِنۢ بَيۡتِهِۦ مُهَاجِرًا إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ثُمَّ يُدۡرِكۡهُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ فَقَدۡ وَقَعَ أَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۗ\nAllah, The Most Generous, will give a full reward to whoever intended to do a good deed but could not achieve it. Al-Biqai: 2/304.\nThis verse indicates Allah's generosity and mercy. Explain.\nوَمَن يَخۡرُجۡ مِنۢ بَيۡتِهِۦ مُهَاجِرًا إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ثُمَّ يُدۡرِكۡهُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ فَقَدۡ وَقَعَ أَجۡرُهُۥ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۗ\nAn immigrant in the cause of Allah will receive one of the two best things: Either he will humiliate the enemies of Allah by parting with them to a place of goodness and abundance, or death will overtake him and he will reach true happiness and eternal bliss. Al-Alusi: 5/128.\nAn immigrant in the cause of Allah will receive one of the two best things. What are they?\nwords\nمُرَاغَمًاA location of refuge\nيَفتِنَكُمُHarm you"],[95,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nFrom the description of the Fear Prayer, deduce a proof that congregational prayer is obligatory, and share it in a message with your colleagues.\nGo to the mosque today at the beginning of prayer time.\nTake steps to be more careful in using communication devices, and do not be heedless of what is conspiring against the Muslims. Taking precaution is an act of worship, and negligence is a sin.\nguid\nA person's heedlessness of what is good for his religion and worldly life is harmful and censured, and it is even worse during wartime.\nA preacher and a fighter in the cause of Allah should compare his patience with that of the people of this world and their endurance of harm for the sake of their worldly objectives; therefore, he must endure for the sake of supporting the truth.\nBeware of supporting the deceitful and defending them even if they were your closest relatives.\nrefl\nوَلۡيَأۡخُذُواْ حِذۡرَهُمۡ وَأَسۡلِحَتَهُمۡۗ\nThis highlights the importance of being alert and cautious of the enemy in all circumstances, and never letting one's guard down, as the army has never suffered a disaster except due to negligence in caution. Al-Qurtubi: 7/109.\nWhy are Muslims ordered to be cautious?\nوَلۡتَأۡتِ طَآئِفَةٌ أُخۡرَىٰ لَمۡ يُصَلُّواْ فَلۡيُصَلُّواْ مَعَكَ وَلۡيَأۡخُذُواْ حِذۡرَهُمۡ\nThis verse indicates that it is preferable to pray behind one Imam, even if that entails neglecting something that would not be neglected if they prayed behind several imams. That is for the sake of uniting Muslims and creating harmony among them, and preventing division, because that is more effective in instilling fear in the hearts of the enemy. Al-Saadi: 198.\nThis verse indicates the importance of unity of Muslims. Explain.\nفَإِذَا سَجَدُواْ فَلۡيَكُونُواْ مِن وَرَآئِكُمۡ وَلۡتَأۡتِ طَآئِفَةٌ أُخۡرَىٰ لَمۡ يُصَلُّواْ فَلۡيُصَلُّواْ مَعَكَ وَلۡيَأۡخُذُواْ حِذۡرَهُمۡ وَأَسۡلِحَتَهُمۡۗ\nThis verse indicates that prayer in congregation is an individual obligation for two reasons: First, Allah enjoined it in these difficult circumstances, at a time of intense fear when the possibility of an enemy attack was very high. If it is enjoined in these difficult circumstances, then it is more appropriate that it should be made obligatory at times of peace and safety. Second, the fact that in the \"Fear Prayer,\" the worshipers omit many conditions and requirements of the prayer, and many actions that would ordinarily nullify other prayers are overlooked, only serves to emphasize the obligatory nature of praying in congregation. If it were not obligatory, it would not be permissible to omit these requirements for the sake of praying in congregation. Al-Saadi: 198.\nHow do you use this verse to prove the obligation of congregational prayer?\nوَخُذُواْ حِذۡرَكُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَذَابٗا مُّهِينٗا ١٠٢\nThe command to be cautious of the enemy may imply its strength and invincibility; therefore, Allah promised victory to Muslims and defeat of the enemy to strengthen their resolve, and so that they would know that taking precaution in itself is an act of worship. Al-Alusi: 5/137.\nWhy does the verse conclude with a threat to the disbelievers?\nفَإِذَا قَضَيۡتُمُ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ فَٱذۡكُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ قِيَٰمٗا وَقُعُودٗا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِكُمۡۚ\nAllah commands Thikr (remembrance of Him) after the Fear Prayer in particular, even though such Thikr is encouraged after other prayers, but here it is more emphasized due to the ease of its pillars and the movement back and forth while performing it, which is unlike other prayers. Ibn Kathir: 1/521.\nWhy is Thikr commanded after the Fear Prayer in particular?\nوَلَا تَهِنُواْ فِي ٱبۡتِغَآءِ ٱلۡقَوۡمِۖ إِن تَكُونُواْ تَأۡلَمُونَ فَإِنَّهُمۡ يَأۡلَمُونَ كَمَا تَأۡلَمُونَۖ وَتَرۡجُونَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَرۡجُونَۗ\nPain should not deter you, because you have a fear of Allah Almighty that should be guarded against more than the guarding against pain. The disbelievers have no fear that makes them bear the pain, but they choose it to promote their false religion. So what is with you and weakness? Al-Alusi: 5/138.\nFear of Allah and hope for His reward prevents the mujahid in the cause of Allah from feeling humiliated. Explain.\nوَلَا تَكُن لِّلۡخَآئِنِينَ خَصِيمٗا ١٠٥\nIslamic scholars said: If the hypocrisy of a people becomes apparent, the Muslims should not argue with each other to protect and defend them, because this happened during the time of the Prophet (r), and it was in them that the verse was revealed: (And do not be an advocate for the deceitful). Al-Qurtubi: 7/116.\nWhat is the ruling of Sharia on defending hypocrites?\nwords\nمَيلَةً وَاحِدَةًIn one single attack to decimate you\nمَوقُوتًاPrescribed at specific times\nابتِغَاءِ القَومِPursuit of the enemy\nخَصِيمًاAn advocate"],[96,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nToday, ask for Allah's forgiveness as much as seventy times, following the example of the Prophet (r).\nRecall a promise you made to yourself but did not keep, and take the initiative to fulfill it.\nName three of Allah's great blessings upon you and thank Him for them, for Allah likes that from you.\nguid\nBeware of committing betrayal and keep away from it, for Allah does not like traitors.\nDo not be of those who fear being seen by others when committing a sin, but they do not fear being seen by Allah.\nIt is a grave sin for one to tell lies about an innocent person, and accuses an honest person of treason.\nrefl\nوَلَا تُجَٰدِلۡ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡتَانُونَ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَن كَانَ خَوَّانًا أَثِيمٗا ١٠٧\nThe (treacherous) is one who betrays repeatedly, and the (sinful) is one who betrays intentionally. Thus, the one who committed treachery once, as well as other acts of treachery that occurred unintentionally or heedlessly are excluded from this definition. Ibn Atiyah: 2/110.\nWhen is a person described as (treacherous)? When is he described as (sinful)?\nوَلَا تُجَٰدِلۡ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡتَانُونَ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَن كَانَ خَوَّانًا أَثِيمٗا ١٠٧\n(Those who betray themselves), they wrong themselves by committing sins. (Indeed, Allah does not like the treacherous and sinful), a frequent traitor who betrays excessively. Abu Hayyan (a prominent interpreter) said: \"The exaggerated form of the Arabic word (treacherous) is used in order to exclude one who committed treachery once, and one who did it unintentionally or heedlessly.\" Al-Alusi: 5/141.\nThe exaggerated form of Arabic word (treacherous) is used. Why?\nوَلَا تُجَٰدِلۡ عَنِ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡتَانُونَ أَنفُسَهُمۡۚ\nThe betrayal of others is described as betrayal of themselves because its evil consequences and harm will return to them. Al-Alusi: 5/140.\nWhy was their betrayal of others described as a betrayal of oneself?\nوَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ سُوٓءًا أَوۡ يَظۡلِمۡ نَفۡسَهُۥ ثُمَّ يَسۡتَغۡفِرِ ٱللَّهَ يَجِدِ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ١١٠\nAli bin Abi Talib (t) said: Abu Bakr (t) told me -and Abu Bakr spoke the truth- he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (r) saying: \" There is no servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution, prays two rak’ahs, and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that he will be forgiven.\" Then he recited this verse: (Whoever commits evil or wrongs himself, then seeks Allah's forgiveness will find Allah All-Forgiving, Most Merciful).\" Al-Qurtubi: 7/117.\nThere are many expiations for sins. Give one example?\nأَوۡ يَظۡلِمۡ نَفۡسَهُۥ\nIt is called wronging oneself because the person's nafs (self) is not his property, such that he may dispose of it as he wishes; rather it is the property of Allah Who has made it a trust with which He has entrusted His servant and enjoined him to keep it (his nafs) on the straight path in word and deed. So, he should strive to teach himself as he has been enjoined and strive to do what is required. Striving to follow any other path is wronging himself, betraying himself, and diverging himself from justice and fairness. Al-Saadi: 201.\nWhy are sins called wronging oneself?\nوَمَن يَكۡسِبۡ إِثۡمٗا فَإِنَّمَا يَكۡسِبُهُۥ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِۦۚ\nIf evil deeds become prevalent and no one objects to them, then the punishment will become widespread and the burden of sin will encompass everyone. That does not contradict the rulings of this verse because whoever abandons the obligatory denunciation has earned a bad deed. Al-Saadi: 201.\nWhen does the punishment of evil affect the perpetrator, and when does it affect society?\nوَمَن يَكۡسِبۡ إِثۡمٗا فَإِنَّمَا يَكۡسِبُهُۥ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِۦۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمٗا ١١١\n(And Allah is All-Knowing, Most Wise) by His knowledge and wisdom, He knows about the sin and what results from it, what prompted it and the punishment that is due for it. He knows the state of the sinner and that if he commits the sin because of the evil inclination of his soul, even though most of the time he is obedient to Allah, He will forgive him and enable him to repent. But if he committed it due to his daring to commit forbidden acts, showing contempt for his Lord and taking His punishment lightly, then this is far from forgiveness and far from success in repentance. Al-Saadi: 201.\nWhat are the two types of sinners?\nwords\nيَختَانُونَThose who betray themselves by committing sins\nخَوَّانًاA treacherous person\nيُبَيِّتُونَThey conspire at night"],[97,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nPreach others today about the virtue of giving charity, or reconcile two disputing parties, seeking the pleasure of Allah.\nAdvise a female relative against plucking her eyebrows or tattooing her body.\nFrom these verses, count the number of ways which satan uses to mislead people. may Allah protect us from him.\nguid\nSocial gatherings are full of ill-speech and backbiting except when it comes to collecting charity, enjoining what is right, or reconciliation between two disputing Muslims.\nBeware of satan luring you and wasting your time and life with false promises and vain hopes.\nBe realistic in your wishes, thoughts and words.\nrefl\nلَّا خَيۡرَ فِي كَثِيرٖ مِّن نَّجۡوَىٰهُمۡ إِلَّا مَنۡ أَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ أَوۡ مَعۡرُوفٍ أَوۡ إِصۡلَٰحِۢ بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِۚ وَمَن يَفۡعَلۡ ذَٰلِكَ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ مَرۡضَاتِ ٱللَّهِ فَسَوۡفَ نُؤۡتِيهِ أَجۡرًا عَظِيمٗا ١١٤\nAl-Awza'i (a prominent scholar) said: There is no step more likable to Allah than the step taken to reconcile between people. Whoever reconciles between two feuding people, Allah will give him an immunity from Hellfire. Al-Qurtubi: 7/129.\nHow important is reconciliation between people? What is its virtue?\nأَوۡ إِصۡلَٰحِۢ بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِۚ\nConflict, disputes and mutual resentment lead to unlimited evil and division. Hence, Allah enjoins bringing about reconciliation between people with regard to matters of blood, wealth and honor, and even when there are differences of religions. Al-Saadi: 202.\nHow important is reconciliation between people?\nوَمَن يُشَاقِقِ ٱلرَّسُولَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ ٱلۡهُدَىٰ وَيَتَّبِعۡ غَيۡرَ سَبِيلِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ نُوَلِّهِۦ مَا تَوَلَّىٰ وَنُصۡلِهِۦ جَهَنَّمَۖ وَسَآءَتۡ مَصِيرًا ١١٥\n(And follows other than the way of the believers): Islamic scholars inferred from this verse that the consensus of Muslims is valid and binding, and that it is not permissible to oppose it. Whoever opposes it, will follow a path other than that of the believers. Ibn Juzay: 1/210.\nIf the Muslims agree unanimously on a matter, it is forbidden to dissent from it. Explain in light of this verse.\nلَّعَنَهُ ٱللَّهُۘ وَقَالَ لَأَتَّخِذَنَّ مِنۡ عِبَادِكَ نَصِيبٗا مَّفۡرُوضٗا ١١٨\nIf someone were to ask: How does satan take a specific portion from among Allah's servants? The answer would be: By misleading them away from the straight path, calling them to follow him, and making misguidance and disbelief attractive to them until he leads them astray from the straight path. Whoever among them answers satan's call and follows his deceit, will become one of satan's specific portion. At-Tabari: 9/212.\nHow does satan take a specific portion from among the servants of Allah?\nوَلَأُضِلَّنَّهُمۡ وَلَأُمَنِّيَنَّهُمۡ\nIt was said that false hopes of satan are inciting them to follow their own whims, to believe that there is no Paradise, Hellfire nor resurrection. Also, that they will enter Paradise in the Hereafter even when continuing to have a sinful life. Al-Baghawi: 1/600.\nWhat are satan's false hopes so that we can avoid them?\nوَلَأٓمُرَنَّهُمۡ فَلَيُغَيِّرُنَّ خَلۡقَ ٱللَّهِۚ\nThis implies that the one who does such actions is discontent with Allah's creation, doubts His wisdom, and believes that what they do with their hands is better than the creation of the Most Merciful, and that they are not content with His decree and creation. Al-Saadi: 204.\nWhy is changing Allah's creation a work of the devil?\nيَعِدُهُمۡ وَيُمَنِّيهِمۡۖ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ إِلَّا غُرُورًا ١٢٠\nMeaning: Delusion is adorning with falsehood, deception, trickery and disguise, showing what has no reality -or has a bad reality- in the most beautiful, noble, and pleasant reality to the soul and most desirable to human nature . Al-Biqai: 2/321.\nWhat is meant by describing satan's promise as delusion?\nwords\nنُوَلِّه مَا تَوَلَّىWe will leave him to what he has chosen\nإِنَاثًاIdols with female names\nمَرِيدًاRebellious\nفَلَيُبَتِّكُنَّThey will slit and cut\nمَحِيصًاAn escape"],[98,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nToday, do something sincere to Allah, do not tell anyone about it, and trust in Allah's promise to you.\nIn order to know how Abraham (u) attained the rank of friendship with Allah, recall today his trials in his closest relatives: His father, son and wife.\nHelp an orphan today with whatever means you have.\nguid\nTrue faith and righteous deed are the key and basis for entering Paradise.\nWhat matters is doing righteous deeds, as for wishing and hoping while neglecting action it is a devil's trick.\nHow many sins you have belittled, but they are significant in the sight of Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ سَنُدۡخِلُهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۖ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٗاۚ وَمَنۡ أَصۡدَقُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ قِيلٗا ١٢٢\nGardens in which there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, nor human heart has ever conceived, of all kinds of delicious food and drinks, wondrous scenes, beautiful spouses, palaces, adorned chambers, amazing trees with low hanging fruit, beautiful voices, and abundant blessings, where people will visit one another and remember the past, all of that in the gardens of paradise. And above all of that and more sublime is the pleasure of Allah upon them. Their souls will enjoy being near to Him, the eyes will enjoy seeing Him, and the ears will enjoy listening to Him, which will make them forget all bliss. Al-Saadi: 205.\nIn Paradise there is bliss that surpasses the bliss of food and drink, what is it?\nمَن يَعۡمَلۡ سُوٓءٗا يُجۡزَ بِهِۦ وَلَا يَجِدۡ لَهُۥ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ وَلِيّٗا وَلَا نَصِيرٗا ١٢٣ وَمَن يَعۡمَلۡ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ مِن ذَكَرٍ أَوۡ أُنثَىٰ وَهُوَ مُؤۡمِنٞ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَدۡخُلُونَ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ\n(Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it): A warning that is inevitable for the disbelievers, but it is constrained by the will of Allah for the Muslims. (And whoever does some righteous deeds): Some righteous deeds, not all of them, because complete righteous deeds are beyond the capability of humans. Ibn Juzay: 1/211.\nIs it a must to do all the righteous deeds to enter Paradise? Why?\nوَمَنۡ أَحۡسَنُ دِينٗا مِّمَّنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ وَٱتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ حَنِيفٗاۗ\nWhen Allah expressed \"submission\" in past tense form, He stipulated continuity and outwardly deeds by saying: (while being a doer of good), meaning: Being a conscious believer and not heedless, rather doer of good is a firmly established quality of his, because he worships Allah as if he were seeing Him. Al-Biqai: 2/324.\nWho is better in religion among the people? Why?\nوَمَنۡ أَحۡسَنُ دِينٗا مِّمَّنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ\nThese two conditions are such that the deed of a servant is not valid without them, that is, it must be sincere and correct. Sincerity means that it is performed for the sake of Allah alone, and correctness means that it conforms to Sharia. Thus, the deed becomes outwardly valid by following Sharia and inwardly valid by sincerity. When a deed lacks either of these two conditions, it becomes null and void. Whoever lacks sincerity is a hypocrite who performs a deed only to be seen by others, and whoever lacks following Sharia is misguided and ignorant. Ibn Kathir: 1/530.\nThe verse indicates two conditions for the acceptance of deeds. What are they?\nوَمَنۡ أَحۡسَنُ دِينٗا مِّمَّنۡ أَسۡلَمَ وَجۡهَهُۥ لِلَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ وَٱتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ حَنِيفٗاۗ وَٱتَّخَذَ ٱللَّهُ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ خَلِيلٗا ١٢٥\nThe one who submitted himself entirely to Allah is he whose intentions are sincerely devoted to Allah, and performs all deeds for His sake. Ibn Taimyah: 2/345.\nWhat is meant by submitting oneself entirely to Allah?\nوَٱتَّخَذَ ٱللَّهُ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ خَلِيلٗا ١٢٥\nThis is an encouragement to follow Abraham Al-Khalil (u), because he is an Imam to be emulated, as he reached the ultimate goal by which servants draw near to Allah. He attained the rank of close friend (Khalil), which is the highest rank of love, and that is due to his great obedience to his Lord. Ibn Kathir: 1/530.\nWhat is the practical benefit to the believer from describing Abraham (u) as a close friend to Allah?\nوَأَن تَقُومُواْ لِلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۚ\nThis includes taking care of them by obligating them to do what Allah has commanded them. Guardians are responsible for that, for making them adhere to that which Allah has made obligatory. This includes taking care of their worldly interests by investing their wealth, handling it only in the best manner, and not approaching it except in the best way. Likewise, they should not do favors to their friends or anyone else at the expense of the orphans, such as giving a girl in their care in marriage to a friend, and so on, in a way that diminishes their rights. This highlights Allah's mercy toward His servants, as He instructs them to look after the interests of those who cannot take care of themselves. Al-Saadi: 206.\nCaring for orphans properly includes two things. What are they?\nwords\nقِيلًاSpeech\nنَقِيرًاThe speck on a date seed\nأَسلَمَSubmitted\nحَنِيفًاInclining toward truth\nخَلِيلًاA close friend"],[99,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nReconcile or participate in reconciling a conflict between two feuding spouses.\nAsk Allah to grant you a sense of fairness and justice, and train yourself to do so.\nThink of something that has made you feel distressed, and ask Allah with His Holy Names: All-Bountiful, All-Wise, to relieve it for you.\nguid\nSettlement in marriage is more favorable to Allah than divorce.\nBeware of giving in to greed and covetousness, and accustom yourself to kindness and generosity.\nDo not make this worldly life your biggest concern.\nrefl\nوَٱلصُّلۡحُ خَيۡرٞۗ وَأُحۡضِرَتِ ٱلۡأَنفُسُ ٱلشُّحَّۚ\nHuman souls are created with an inclination toward stinginess, which makes the individual reluctant to give what is due to others, and eager to obtain what is due to himself. Souls are naturally inclined toward that; therefore, you should strive to eradicate this vile trait from your souls and replace it with its opposite, which is tolerance and generosity. That means giving what is due to others and being content with some of that to which you are entitled. Al-Saadi: 207.\nWhat is the definition of stinginess? And how to rid oneself of it?\nوَأُحۡضِرَتِ ٱلۡأَنفُسُ ٱلشُّحَّۚ وَإِن تُحۡسِنُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ خَبِيرٗا ١٢٨\n(But if you do good) meaning: Be a doer of good by remaining in marriage and treating your wives with kindness, even if you are reluctant. (And fear Allah), that is: Be pious by avoiding everything that causes harm, indicating that the stingy person is neither a doer of good nor pious. (Then indeed Allah is ever, of what you do, Aware) meaning: Allah is fully aware of your deeds, and since He is the Most Generous, He will give you the best reward for it. Al-Biqai: 2/329.\nThe requital befits the action. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَإِن تُصۡلِحُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ١٢٩\n(If you do what is right) between you and your wives by forcing yourselves to do what you do not like, seeking reward and fulfilling the rights of your wives. (Allah is surely All-Forgiving, Most Merciful): He will forgive the sins and shortcomings you have committed in fulfilling the obligatory rights, and He will have mercy on you as you have been kind to your wives and shown them compassion. Al-Saadi: 207.\nWhat is the reward for a husband's kindness and compassion toward his wife?\nوَلَن تَسۡتَطِيعُوٓاْ أَن تَعۡدِلُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ وَلَوۡ حَرَصۡتُمۡۖ فَلَا تَمِيلُواْ كُلَّ ٱلۡمَيۡلِ\nDo not wrong the wife that you are not interested in by inclining toward another wife, and depriving her of her right without her consent, and be as just in treating them as you can. The fact that you will not be able to achieve absolute justice between your wives does not prevent you from being charged with lesser mandates that you are capable of. Al-Alusi: 5/162.\nIs the inability to achieve absolute justice a justification for wrongdoing?\nوَلَن تَسۡتَطِيعُوٓاْ أَن تَعۡدِلُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ وَلَوۡ حَرَصۡتُمۡۖ فَلَا تَمِيلُواْ كُلَّ ٱلۡمَيۡلِ فَتَذَرُوهَا كَٱلۡمُعَلَّقَةِۚ وَإِن تُصۡلِحُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ١٢٩\n(And you will never be able to maintain absolute justice between your wives), that is a complete and perfect justice in words, actions, emotions, and other things, which are unattainable by people, so Allah relieved them from this obligation. Ibn Juzay: 1/213.\nWhat justice cannot a husband do between his wives?\nإِن يَشَأۡ يُذۡهِبۡكُمۡ أَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ وَيَأۡتِ بِـَٔاخَرِينَۚ\nSome righteous predecessors said: \"How insignificant the people become in the sight of Allah when they disobey Him.\" Ibn Kathir: 1/535.\nWhat is the true value of a human being in the sight of Allah,the Almighty?\nمَّن كَانَ يُرِيدُ ثَوَابَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا فَعِندَ ٱللَّهِ ثَوَابُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ\n(Then with Allah), He Who Has absolute perfection. (The reward of this world), this lowly and mortal life. (And of the Hereafter), the precious and everlasting life. Thus, whoever wants either of these rewards, should ask Allah, for He gives to whomever He chooses whatever He wills. And whoever's aspiration is higher than that, turning his heart to Allah, limiting his concern to Him, and seeking only the Hereafter, the Almighty will combine both rewards for him. Likewise, when he strives sincerely in the cause of Allah, Allah will combine for him the reward and the spoils. Al-Biqai: 2/333.\nWhat is meant by (Then with Allah is the reward of this world and of the Hereafter)?\nwords\nنُشُوزًاContempt\nوَأُحضِرَتِ الأَنفُسُ الشُّحَّHuman souls are prone to stinginess\nفَتَذَرُوهَاLeaving her\nكَالمُعَلَّقَةِNeither married nor divorced"],[100,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you power, knowing that it comes only from Him.\nGather the pillars of faith found in the verse, then ask your Lord to fulfill them for you.\nShare a message in which you warn against movie actors who mock Allah's religion and His allies.\nguid\nJustice is one of the most important qualities of the believers and Ahl As-Sunnah, so stand firm in it.\nBeware of following your whims, as it will lead to heedlessness and destruction.\nConsider how Allah mentions the hypocrites before the disbelievers due to their cunning and extreme danger.\nrefl\nإِن يَكُنۡ غَنِيًّا أَوۡ فَقِيرٗا فَٱللَّهُ أَوۡلَىٰ بِهِمَاۖ\nThe wealth or poverty of either party in the dispute should not be a reason to judge or testify for or against him. The purpose of this is to warn against being influenced by doubtful situations in which falsehood is confused with truth because of the circumstances surrounding them, which are perceived to be a form of establishing interests and protecting justice. Ibn Ashur: 5/226.\nDoes the wealth or poverty of either party in the dispute influence the judge's ruling or the witness' testimony?\nفَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ ٱلۡهَوَىٰٓ أَن تَعۡدِلُواْۚ وَإِن تَلۡوُۥٓاْ أَوۡ تُعۡرِضُواْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ خَبِيرٗا ١٣٥\nFollowing desires is destructive. Allah says, (So judge between people with justice, and do not follow your desires lest they lead you astray from Allah's way) [38:26]. Following one's desires leads one to testify against the truth, to be unjust in judgment, and other things. Ash-Shaabi (a prominent scholar) said: \"Allah obligated the rulers/judges with three things: They must not follow desires, must not fear people, and must not trade the verses of Allah [truth] for a small price.\" Al-Qurtubi: 7/178.\nShould the richness or poverty of either party in the dispute influences the witness testimony or the judgement?\nفَلَا تَتَّبِعُواْ ٱلۡهَوَىٰٓ أَن تَعۡدِلُواْۚ\nDesires will either make a person blind so that he sees the truth as false and sees falsehood as truth, or he may recognize the truth but fail to follow it because of his desires. Al-Saadi: 209.\nDescribe the risk associated with following one's desires?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَتَّخِذُونَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَۚ أَيَبۡتَغُونَ عِندَهُمُ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ فَإِنَّ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعٗا ١٣٩\nAllah mentions the worst trait of hypocrites, which is taking the disbelievers as allies instead of the believers. He has warned of the corruption of that so that any of the believers who might fall into that type of thing, out of negligence, ignorance, or leniency, may abandon it. Ibn-Atiyah: 2/125.\nThe traits of hypocrites are all harmful to Muslims; which one is the worst?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَتَّخِذُونَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَۚ أَيَبۡتَغُونَ عِندَهُمُ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ فَإِنَّ ٱلۡعِزَّةَ لِلَّهِ جَمِيعٗا ١٣٩\nAll power belongs to Allah, to His Messenger and to the believers, but the hypocrites do not know. This is meant to encourage the servants to seek power from Allah, turn to His servitude, and join the ranks of His faithful servants. Ibn Kathir: 1/536.\nWhat is meant by Allah telling His servants that all power belongs to Him?\nوَقَدۡ نَزَّلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أَنۡ إِذَا سَمِعۡتُمۡ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ يُكۡفَرُ بِهَا وَيُسۡتَهۡزَأُ بِهَا فَلَا تَقۡعُدُواْ مَعَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَخُوضُواْ فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيۡرِهِۦٓ\nThis verse from Surat Al-An'am (When you see those who ridicule Our verses, turn away from them until they engage in another discourse) was revealed in Makkah, so it was limited to merely turning away and boycotting the gathering, because the believers were unable to repudiate it except with their hearts. However, this verse was revealed in Madinah, so repudiation now is possible for every Muslim with words and actions, since sitting with them without repudiating is considered a consent. Al-Biqai: 2/337.\nIn Surat Al-An'am, Allah commands the believers to turn away, but in this Surah, He commands not to sit with them. Why?\nوَقَدۡ نَزَّلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أَنۡ إِذَا سَمِعۡتُمۡ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ يُكۡفَرُ بِهَا وَيُسۡتَهۡزَأُ بِهَا فَلَا تَقۡعُدُواْ مَعَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَخُوضُواْ فِي حَدِيثٍ غَيۡرِهِۦٓ إِنَّكُمۡ إِذٗا مِّثۡلُهُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ جَامِعُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيعًا ١٤٠\n(In Hell): Which is the King's prison. (Together): Just as the assembly of disbelief, which is a challenge to the King's reign, brought them together in this worldly life. For sitting together, they became equal in disbelief, which proves that sitting with a sinner without repudiating his sin makes one a sinner too. Al-Biqai: 2/337.\nAllah will gather all the hypocrites and disbelievers in Hellfire together. Why?\nwords\nقَوَّامِينَStanding firm\nبِالقِسطِIn justice\nتَلوُواYou distort [the testimony]\nتُعرِضُواYou decline [to testify]"],[101,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nGo to prayer early today with diligence and devotion, and do not be like the hypocrites.\nRemember Allah often today and glorify Him, starting with morning and evening Athkar then with general Athkar.\nShare a message in which you remind others to be steadfast, to keep company with the righteous, and not to waver in religion, as this is a characteristic of hypocrites.\nguid\nReluctance to stand up and be ready for prayer is a sign of hypocrisy so beware of that.\nReluctance and hesitation to join good believers is a trait of hypocrites, so do not be among them.\nGuidance is only from Allah, so ask Him to guide you and your family.\nrefl\nفَإِن كَانَ لَكُمۡ فَتۡحٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ قَالُوٓاْ أَلَمۡ نَكُن مَّعَكُمۡ وَإِن كَانَ لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ نَصِيبٞ\n(But if the disbelievers have a share), Allah did not say victory, because they do not attain victory in the sense of permanently prevailing; rather it is just an unstable share of success. Al-Saadi: 210.\nWhy is the victory of the believers described as a (victory), and the victory of the disbelievers described as a (share)?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ يُخَٰدِعُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَهُوَ خَٰدِعُهُمۡ وَإِذَا قَامُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ قَامُواْ كُسَالَىٰ يُرَآءُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ وَلَا يَذۡكُرُونَ ٱللَّهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ١٤٢\nThese reprehensible traits indicate that the believers are characterized by their opposites, namely sincerity and truthfulness, both outward and inward. No one is ignorant of what they have, their vigor in their prayers and worship, their frequent remembrance of Allah, and that He has guided them to the straight path. So let the wise person think about these two groups and choose whichever of them he wants. And Allah is the one sought for help. Al-Saadi: 211.\nHow do you infer the believers' qualities from these verses?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ يُخَٰدِعُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَهُوَ خَٰدِعُهُمۡ وَإِذَا قَامُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ قَامُواْ كُسَالَىٰ يُرَآءُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ\nMeaning: The hypocrite find the prayer burdensome, and have no desire to do it because they do not believe that there is a reward for establishing prayer, nor a punishment for omitting it. Al-Alusi: 5/175.\nWhy are the hypocrites reluctant to pray?\nوَلَا يَذۡكُرُونَ ٱللَّهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ١٤٢\nBecause they [the hypocrites] remember Allah only with their tongues, and in the presence of other people. Unlike true believers, who, when they stand up to pray, they hasten to it with the wings of hope and fear, and they yearn for its times. Al-Alusi: 5/181.\nThe hypocrites do not remember Allah but a little. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَۚ أَتُرِيدُونَ أَن تَجۡعَلُواْ لِلَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ سُلۡطَٰنٗا مُّبِينًا ١٤٤\nMeaning: A clear proof that those who do that will be punished. This indicates that Allah in His wisdom does not punish anyone until after the evidence is established against him, and this rule is evidenced by many verses of the Quran. It is also said: By taking the disbelievers as allies, do you want to make clear evidence to Allah that you are hypocrites, for taking the disbelievers as allies is the clearest evidence of hypocrisy. Al-Alusi: 5/177.\nThis verse is a proof that Allah, the Almighty, is Just. Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ فِي ٱلدَّرۡكِ ٱلۡأَسۡفَلِ مِنَ ٱلنَّارِ وَلَن تَجِدَ لَهُمۡ نَصِيرًا ١٤٥\nThe lowest depth of the Fire is the most hidden and wicked part of it, just as their disbelief is the most hidden and wicked type of disbelief. Al-Biqai: 2/340.\nWhy will the hypocrites be in the lowest depths of Hellfire?\nمَّا يَفۡعَلُ ٱللَّهُ بِعَذَابِكُمۡ إِن شَكَرۡتُمۡ وَءَامَنتُمۡۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ شَاكِرًا عَلِيمٗا ١٤٧\nGratitude is mentioned before faith because the servant reflects on the favors and becomes grateful, then believes in the One Who bestowed them, so gratitude is a cause of faith and precedes it. Ibn Juzay: 1/216.\nGratitude precedes faith in this verse: (If you are grateful and faithful). Why?\nwords\nالَّذِينَ يَتَرَبَّصُونَ بِكُمThose who are waiting and watching to see what happens to you\nنَستَحوِذ عَلَيكُمWe are with you\nمُذَبذَبِينَWavering and reluctant\nالدَّركِAn abyss"],[102,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nSpeak only good words today, such as welcoming words, Thikr (remembrance of Allah), inviting others to do good deeds, so that it becomes a habit for you, for Allah likes that.\nRecall a bad word that you are habitually using , and replace it with a good one and use it often.\nPardon someone, today, who wronged you by words or action because if you do, Allah Will pardon you.\nguid\nFaith is belief, discipline and good manners.\nIt is desirable to consistently speak good words while being aware that Allah hears you.\nPardoning others is a cause for Allah's forgiveness of your sins.\nrefl\nلَّا يُحِبُّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡجَهۡرَ بِٱلسُّوٓءِ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ إِلَّا مَن ظُلِمَۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ سَمِيعًا عَلِيمًا ١٤٨\n(Except by one who has been wronged), the oppressed is the only one who is permitted to utter offensive words publicly, to invoke Allah's wrath upon the oppressor, to speaks publicly of his injustice, or to respond to his oppressor with the same insults if any were directed at him. Ibn Juzay: 1/216.\nWhen is uttering offensive words in public permitted?\nلَّا يُحِبُّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡجَهۡرَ بِٱلسُّوٓءِ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ\nThis indicates that Allah loves good words such as Thikr and kind gentle words. Al-Saadi: 212.\nIn light of this verse, how do we know that Allah loves good words?\nلَّا يُحِبُّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡجَهۡرَ بِٱلسُّوٓءِ مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡلِ إِلَّا مَن ظُلِمَۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ سَمِيعًا عَلِيمًا ١٤٨\nAllah permits for the oppressed to utter offensive words in public to clear his anger so he does not revert to using his sword or hands. Ibn Ashur: 6/6.\nIslamic Sharia advocates inflicting the lesser of the two evils. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِن تُبۡدُواْ خَيۡرًا أَوۡ تُخۡفُوهُ أَوۡ تَعۡفُواْ عَن سُوٓءٖ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَفُوّٗا قَدِيرًا ١٤٩\nThis is an encouragement to do good deeds in public and in private, and to forgive an offense after retaliation is permitted because pardoning is more likable to Allah than retaliation, and He affirmed this by describing Himself as Ever-Pardoning and Most Capable. Ibn Juzay: 1/216.\nPardoning and retaliation: which one is permitted? Which one is more likable to Allah?\nأَوۡ تَعۡفُواْ عَن سُوٓءٖ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَفُوّٗا قَدِيرًا ١٤٩\n(Or pardon an offense) means that you pardon someone who mistreated you physically, financially, or by impugning your honor, and you forgive him because the reward is commensurate with the type of deed. If a person forgives for the sake of Allah, Allah will forgive him; if he shows kindness, Allah will be kind to him. In this verse, a guidance to learn the meanings of the Names and Attributes of Allah, and the fact that creation and command commence from them. Therefore, the rulings are reasoned by His Holy Names as it is clear in this verse. Al-Saadi: 212.\nThe rulings in the Quran are mostly reasoned by Allah's Holy Names. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَن يُفَرِّقُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦ وَيَقُولُونَ نُؤۡمِنُ بِبَعۡضٖ وَنَكۡفُرُ بِبَعۡضٖ وَيُرِيدُونَ أَن يَتَّخِذُواْ بَيۡنَ ذَٰلِكَ سَبِيلًا ١٥٠ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ حَقّٗاۚ وَأَعۡتَدۡنَا لِلۡكَٰفِرِينَ عَذَابٗا مُّهِينٗا ١٥١\nAllah threatens the disbelievers in Him and in His Messengers from among Jews and Christians, who make a distinction between Allah and His Messengers. They believe in some Prophets and reject others, following their whims, desires and the practices of their forefathers. They do not follow any proof for such distinction, because there is no such proof. Rather, they follow their whims and prejudices. Ibn Kathir: 1/541.\nThis verse makes clear the ruling on whoever claims that he believes in Allah but not in His Messengers or some of them. Explain.\nيَسۡـَٔلُكَ أَهۡلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أَن تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ كِتَٰبٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِۚ فَقَدۡ سَأَلُواْ مُوسَىٰٓ أَكۡبَرَ مِن ذَٰلِكَ فَقَالُوٓاْ أَرِنَا ٱللَّهَ جَهۡرَةٗ فَأَخَذَتۡهُمُ ٱلصَّٰعِقَةُ بِظُلۡمِهِمۡۚ ثُمَّ ٱتَّخَذُواْ ٱلۡعِجۡلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَتۡهُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتُ فَعَفَوۡنَا عَن ذَٰلِكَۚ وَءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَىٰ سُلۡطَٰنٗا مُّبِينٗا ١٥٣\nAllah's Messengers cannot answer their people's requests for miracles, but miracles come by the will of Allah when His Messengers were challenged. If Allah answered every request for a miracle, His Messengers would be like magicians responding to people's requests at public and private gatherings, which is demeaning to the status of Prophethood. Ibn Ashur: 6/14.\nThis verse is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ). Explain.\nwords\nالطُّورَA mountain in Sinai\nلاَ تَعدُواDo not transgress"],[103,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to set right your heart, and seek refuge with Him from a sealed heart that leads to blindness, confusion and misguidance.\nShare a message in which you document some of the crimes committed by the Jews to warn others of their evil.\nShare a message in which you defend sincere scholars, reformers and righteous people, for Allah defends His allies and obedient servants.\nguid\nAccusing chaste women falsely is one of the seven sins that doom one to Hellfire.\nStrive in pursuing knowledge and increasing your faith so that you become among those who are firm in knowledge.\nThe Quran's recurring emphasis on prayer and zakah confirms their great importance so be mindful of them.\nrefl\nفَبِمَا نَقۡضِهِم مِّيثَٰقَهُمۡ وَكُفۡرِهِم بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَقَتۡلِهِمُ ٱلۡأَنۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖ وَقَوۡلِهِمۡ قُلُوبُنَا غُلۡفُۢ بَلۡ طَبَعَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهَا بِكُفۡرِهِمۡ فَلَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ١٥٥\nThis is the best way to counter arguments that are founded on an invalid basis. If an opponent produces a false argument that becomes a source of confusion to him and others causing them to reject the truth, we should highlight his evil characteristics and some of his worst misdeeds, so that everyone will know that this objection comes from this ignoble man, and that he has past misdeeds along with this invalid argument of his. Al-Saadi: 214.\nThis verse describes a way on how to respond to corruptors. Explain.\nوَقَوۡلِهِمۡ إِنَّا قَتَلۡنَا ٱلۡمَسِيحَ عِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ رَسُولَ ٱللَّهِ\nMeaning: We killed the person who claimed to be the Messenger of Allah. The Jews only uttered these words in jest and mockery, just as the polytheists said: (O you to whom the Reminder (The Quran) has been sent down, you are surely insane) [15:6]. Ibn Kathir: 1/543.\nThis verse mentions that Jews combined two major sins. What were they?\nوَقَوۡلِهِمۡ إِنَّا قَتَلۡنَا ٱلۡمَسِيحَ عِيسَى ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ رَسُولَ ٱللَّهِ وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوهُ وَلَٰكِن شُبِّهَ لَهُمۡۚ وَإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱخۡتَلَفُواْ فِيهِ لَفِي شَكّٖ مِّنۡهُۚ مَا لَهُم بِهِۦ مِنۡ عِلۡمٍ إِلَّا ٱتِّبَاعَ ٱلظَّنِّۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ يَقِينَۢا ١٥٧\nAllah enumerates their ugly sins such as saying: (We killed the Messiah) because they said that audaciously with pride even though they were lying; nevertheless, the guilt clung to them although they did not actually kill him but crucified another person whom Allah cast resemblance of Jesus on him, and they thought they killed Jesus. Ibn Juzay: 1/217.\nThe claim made by the Jews that they killed the Messiah, even though they actually did not, is considered among their ugly sins. Why?\nوَمَا قَتَلُوهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوهُ وَلَٰكِن شُبِّهَ لَهُمۡۚ وَإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱخۡتَلَفُواْ فِيهِ لَفِي شَكّٖ مِّنۡهُۚ مَا لَهُم بِهِۦ مِنۡ عِلۡمٍ إِلَّا ٱتِّبَاعَ ٱلظَّنِّۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوهُ يَقِينَۢا ١٥٧\n(But they did not kill him nor did they crucify him), this is a response and a refutation to the Jews and Christians for saying that he was crucified, and they ended up worshiping the crucifix. What is astonishing is their contradiction in saying that he is a god or a son of god then they say he was crucified. Ibn Juzay: 1/217.\nShow the contradiction in the beliefs of Christians?\nبَل رَّفَعَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِلَيۡهِۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمٗا ١٥٨\nSince He is the All-Mighty, He honors and protects His allies, and being the All-Wise, He perfected the ascent of Jesus to make it a trial for the disbelievers and a source of insight to the believers. Ibn Ashur: 6/24.\nThis verse concludes with (and Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise). Why?\nفَبِظُلۡمٖ مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَادُواْ حَرَّمۡنَا عَلَيۡهِمۡ طَيِّبَٰتٍ أُحِلَّتۡ لَهُمۡ وَبِصَدِّهِمۡ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ كَثِيرٗا ١٦٠\nAllah states that He prohibited to the people of the Book many good things that had previously been permissible for them. This prohibition was a punishment for their wrongdoing and transgression, turning people away from the path of Allah, preventing them from following true guidance, and consumption of usury although it was forbidden to them, thus depriving those who need to trade with them from fairness. Hence, Allah gave them a fitting punishment by withholding from them many of the good things that were originally permitted, even though they are good. In the case of the things that are prohibited to the Muslim nation, this prohibition is to keep them away from unclean things that are detrimental to their spiritual and worldly interests. Al-Saadi: 214.\nWhat is the difference between what is prohibited to us and that which is to the Jews?\nلَّٰكِنِ ٱلرَّٰسِخُونَ فِي ٱلۡعِلۡمِ مِنۡهُمۡ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ مِن قَبۡلِكَۚ وَٱلۡمُقِيمِينَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَۚ وَٱلۡمُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ سَنُؤۡتِيهِمۡ أَجۡرًا عَظِيمًا ١٦٢\nHaving mentioned the bad characteristics of the people of the Book, Allah, then, mentions those among them who are praiseworthy, as He says, (But those firm in knowledge among them) that is, those in whose hearts knowledge is deeply entrenched and faith is firmly rooted. That resulted in them having complete faith (in what has been revealed to you, [O Prophet], and what was revealed before you). Moreover, it resulted in them doing righteous deeds, namely establishing prayer and giving zakah, which are the best of deeds that manifested sincerity toward Allah and kindness toward people. Al-Saadi: 214.\nHow can you distinguish between those who are firm in knowledge and other scholars?\nwords\nغُلفٌWrapped up\nالرَّاسِخُونَFirm (in knowledge)"]])